   "text": {
    "L1": "A life cycle is the series of stages a living thing passes through. It ends with an adult that can reproduce, so the cycle repeats.",
    "L2": "A seed first germinates, then becomes a seedling. The seedling grows into an adult plant that makes flowers, fruits and new seeds.",
    "L3": "A mosquito has four separate stages: egg, larva, pupa and adult. Eggs are laid on still water, and larvae and pupae live there.",
    "L4": "A frog begins as eggs in water. The tadpole has gills and a tail, then legs appear, the tail shrinks and lungs form.",
    "L5": "The froglet becomes an adult frog that lives on land and in water. The adult lays eggs again.",
    "L6": "A tadpole and an adult frog are the same animal at different stages. This big change in body form is called metamorphosis.",
    "L7": "Now put the mosquito stages in their life-cycle order."
   },
